    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1067-a1">

                <pb facs="1159" n="1063" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1063"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Villa Marguerite</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Valescure, St.
                                Raphael, Var, France</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-02-19"><hi rendition="#italic">February 19,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear White</hi>: As an outsider, and in the
                    absence of your ambassador, permit me to write one line to you to express my
                    horror at the fearful accident that has happened to the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Maine</hi>. It is bad enough for men-of-war to founder with all their <pb
                        facs="1160" n="1064" xml:id="pg1064"/> crews, but to be blown up into the
                    air is too horrible. I do not for a moment think that it was malicious—merely an
                    accident; but the horror remains the same.</p>
                <p>I am sure you will receive the sympathy of the whole British nation, and I can
                    not refrain from writing to say what I feel.</p>
                <p>Yours, very sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Abercorn.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
